% parameters.clausal -- the PROVENANCE records of the sourced figures of
% eu/dora_rts_logging_and_network_security. PROVENANCE ONLY: this file references each figure by
% name and holds no value, and the logic modules do not import it.
%
% If parameters-sources.yaml is the COMMISSIONING REGISTER (its first line
% says so), then for EACH of its keys:
%   1. the VALUE is a fact in the determination slice that READS it
%      (that slice's .clausal file), never here;
%   2. this file holds its provenance record, a fact:
%        parameter_source(<key>, [label-'...', ref-'...', verbatim-'...']).
%      with the verbatim pair OMITTED while the yaml entry is
%   `status: unverified`.
% Otherwise this file holds no records at the baseline.
%
% This order holds NO statutory figure. The frequencies of the text
% (RTS Art 13(i) 'once a year' and 'periodically'; Art 13 closing
% subparagraph 'on a regular basis' and 'at least every 6 months';
% Art 14(1)(c) 'regularly reviewed') are part of the caller's judgement
% of the duty they belong to (reading (9), open question (Q10)): the
% order reads no date and computes no interval, so no figure is read by
% any rule and no parameter_source record is written.
% =====================================================================

:- module(parameters, []).

:- end_module(parameters).
